-66508" :question/problem "![](images/23/239490fd3be930412d4f67ff89244607a5019d91f201bc4e579410b5610a18ed.png)\n\nWhich of the graphs above correspond to an invertible function?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible if and only if it's a one-to-one function. To determine which of the functions are one-to-one, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n![](images/c7/c728d173c13a1e7b3bcad0e9f0284c97f2ca075c795dcb1f38ed086c19cc0504.png)\n\nFrom the above, we see that: \n\n- For graphs I and IV, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line. Therefore, graphs I  and IV show one-to-one functions. This means that  these functions are invertible.\n\n- For graphs II and  III, some horizontal lines intersect the curve more than once. So, these are not one-to-one functions. As a result, they are not invertible."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403244 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7166ecf3-b50b-508e-9ed3-8ed61ef5ae61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438382} {:answer/id #uuid "f55eb19c-2f9e-55bf-96bf-393b353a9fa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438383}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7166ecf3-b50b-508e-9ed3-8ed61ef5ae61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438382} :answer-field/id #uuid "83c282a3-ae0f-5137-bd44-fd265e629295" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439220} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e4146f84-975f-51a7-8ac3-491200ec7ad8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438384} {:answer/id #uuid "95464e11-21eb-5